<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elias Lönnrot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1802–1884</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elias Lönnrot was a Finnish physician and philologist who collected oral folk poetry on long journeys through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> and compiled from it the national epic, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalevala">Kalevala</a>, published in 1835 and enlarged in 1849. He also compiled a great Finnish–Swedish dictionary and helped develop Finnish as a written language, later teaching it as a professor at the University of Helsinki.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elias-lonnrot.jpg" alt="Elias Lönnrot" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elias_Lönnrot_potrait.jpg: unknwon derivative work: Bff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elias_L%C3%B6nnrot_portrait-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
